/*
 * Sunfish Divers: the ocean engine (js/ocean.js)
 * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 * One dependency-free script shared by all nine pages. Works from file://.
 *
 *   1  Art table (embedded creature SVGs)      7  Sea life by depth
 *   2  Helpers and shared state                8  Bubbles (streams and bursts)
 *   3  Depth system (--depth on <html>)        9  Torch (wreck zone, mouse only)
 *   4  Water and light layers inside #ocean   10  Site behaviour (header, menu,
 *   5  Depth HUD                                  reveal, tone, photos, year,
 *   6  Tone (light / dark panels)                 filter, enquiry form,
 *                                                 phone action bar)
 *                                             11  Boot
 *
 * Phones (under 700 px wide, state.small) get a lighter engine: the sea life
 * has no parallax, so nothing but the water and the light is restyled while
 * scrolling; the sunfish is given a clearing of open water; and the home
 * wreck becomes a short tour (section 7, "Phones").
 *
 * Rules of the house
 * - The scroll handler is passive and rAF-throttled and reads only scrollY.
 *   Everything that depends on layout is measured on load / resize / when the
 *   document height changes, and cached.
 * - Only transform and opacity are animated or transitioned. Fades by depth
 *   are CSS expressions of --depth (see css/styles.css, "OCEAN ENGINE").
 * - No console output, no dependencies, no network requests.
 * - Every feature no-ops when its markup is missing.
 * - prefers-reduced-motion: no swimming, parallax, bubbles, rays, drift or
 *   torch; the colour descent, the HUD, tone and static sea life stay.
 */
